{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794818160,"nonce":"yjGc7S9K90wQrpEMf93jeyw7nb8=","title":"Rows lose ordered images and float canvases on the cn_demo page","message":"With the clip split (ba9cdf06) and the stack / nested-scroll guard removed, the user saw two regressions in cn_demo:\n\n1. The avatars disappear when scrolling stops in the Avatar section (visible while scrolling, back on hover or click). Headless, the page's dynamic batch there has ordered images (`has_ordered_images`: images drawn through the paint context's `emit_image`, paint_order set), so `NodeRows::plan` declines at every adopt (`has_ordered_content`). After a decline the motion image list ends up not drawn by any pass until a full paint is forced (the latent bug noted on 8bcd6ab: `patched == false` clears cached_motion_subtree_images and the adopt then runs with images None).\n2. Charts (canvases in cards) float out of place while scrolling. Rows replay of canvases (`replay_rows_canvases`) pushed the clip recorded at paint before the row affine and gave the replayed primitives only the painted node_slot, not the painted clip (now copied, unverified in a window). Path vertices under an inner clip took a shape pointer, which made the batch ordered too (now kept as a plain clip rect).\n\nThe guard is back (stack layer, nested scroll keep a container off rows) so the page is painted as it scrolls. To lift it: let rows take batches with ordered images (move them with their row or replay them), fix the image list being lost after a decline, verify canvases in cards in a window, and get a headless reproduction: COSTS_AT=Avatar COSTS_ASYNC=1 COSTS_SNAP=\u003cpng\u003e in tools/blinc-bench cn_demo_costs lands at the wrong part of the page (the snapshot showed Form Inputs), which needs fixing before it can serve.","files":null}]}